{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f0a1b2c3-d4e5-6789-0abc-def123456789",
    "name": "Axis Assistant API",
    "description": "API collection for the Axis Assistant platform.\n\n**Auth model**\n- **Public (dashboard-facing)** endpoints under `/api/v1/*` do **not** require `X-API-Key`.\n- **Internal (agent → backend)** endpoints under `/api/v1/internal/*` require the service-to-service key: `X-API-Key: {{service_api_key}}`.\n- **Agent direct** calls (calling the Python service directly) also require: `X-API-Key: {{service_api_key}}`.\n\n**Approvals**\nThe product no longer uses a human approval flow. The backend may still expose approval endpoints for legacy/testing, but they are intentionally omitted from this collection to avoid confusion.\n\n**Response envelope**\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": { },\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"meta\": { \"request_id\": \"...\", \"timestamp\": \"...\" }\n}\n```\n\n**Error codes**\n- `backend.*` — Go backend\n- `agent.*` — Python agent\n- `external.*` — third-party\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Health check endpoints for both services.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Backend Health Check",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "No auth required. Returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` if the Go backend is running."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Agent Health Check",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{agent_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{agent_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "No auth required. Returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` from the Python agent."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Chat",
      "description": "Chat endpoints — the main conversational interface.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send Message",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Ensure session_id is set",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('session_id')) {",
                  "  console.warn('⚠️ session_id is empty. Create a session first.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"{{session_id}}\",\n  \"message\": \"What's on my calendar today?\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/chat",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "chat"]
            },
            "description": "Send a message to the agent via the Go backend proxy.\n\nRequires an active `session_id` (use Sessions > Create Session).\n\nNote: the approval flow is removed, so `requires_approval` should be `false`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
